.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH UNIPROT 1 2000-1月 "subcellular_location" "subcellular_location"
.SH NAME
subcellular_location \- Extract the sub-cellular location information as a GSEA background model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIsubcellular_location(\fBuniprot\fR as any, 
\fBdb_xref\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Extract the sub-cellular location information as a GSEA background model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBuniprot\fB \fR\- 
 a collection of the UniProt protein [entry](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Assembly.Uniprot.XML.entry) data, or a file path of the
 UniProt database xml file.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdb_xref\fB \fR\- 
 the database cross reference name that will be used as the gene id of the background
 members, for example \fBGeneID\fR. Default \fBNULL\fR means using the UniProt accession id.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [Background](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.Background) model whose clusters are the sub-cellular locations and the
 members are the proteins that are annotated in each location, or an error message when
 the input data could not be cast into the UniProt entry collection.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
UniProt
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
